drivers/staging/android/ion: fix use-before-init in the deferred
free list drain (kswapd NULL deref in ion_heap_shrink_scan)

OPLUS added a task_struct memleak-accounting block to
_ion_heap_freelist_drain() above the loop that assigns `buffer`, i.e.
it dereferences an uninitialized pointer.  clang-14 propagates the
poison into the arm64 LL/SC atomics and emits a put_task_struct()
sequence whose address register is never loaded, so any shrinker run
with a non-empty DEFER_FREE freelist panics kswapd0.

Drop the block: it is a duplicate of the accounting ion_buffer_destroy()
already performs for every buffer drained here, so removing it also
avoids a double put_task_struct().  No exported symbol, data layout or
ABI CRC changes.

---
--- a/drivers/staging/android/ion/ion_heap.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/android/ion/ion_heap.c
@@ -193,13 +193,25 @@
 	if (ion_heap_freelist_size(heap) == 0)
 		return 0;
 
-#if defined(OPLUS_FEATURE_MEMLEAK_DETECT) && defined(CONFIG_DUMP_TASKS_MEM)
-	if (buffer->tsk) {
-		atomic64_sub(buffer->size, &buffer->tsk->ions);
-		put_task_struct(buffer->tsk);
-		buffer->tsk = NULL;
-	}
-#endif
+	/*
+	 * Do not touch buffer->tsk here: the loop below is what assigns
+	 * "buffer", so at this point the pointer is uninitialized.  Reading it
+	 * is undefined behaviour, and clang-14 propagates the poison straight
+	 * into the LL/SC atomic templates of put_task_struct():
+	 *
+	 *   prfm pstl1strm, [x8]; ldxr x8, [x8]; sub x8, x8, x8;
+	 *   stxr w9, x8, [x8]; ...; bl __put_task_struct
+	 *
+	 * x8 is never loaded from anything, so it holds a stale caller-saved
+	 * value (0 after _raw_spin_unlock) and kswapd dies in
+	 * ion_heap_shrink_scan with "Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer
+	 * dereference at virtual address 00000000".
+	 *
+	 * The accounting is not needed here either: ion_buffer_destroy() below
+	 * already subtracts buffer->size from buffer->tsk->ions, drops the
+	 * task_struct reference and clears buffer->tsk for every buffer this
+	 * loop drains.  Keeping the block would double put_task_struct().
+	 */
 	spin_lock(&heap->free_lock);
 	if (size == 0)
 		size = heap->free_list_size;
